#text(weight: "bold")[Application — Cloud Native Architect, Strategic Accounts (EMEA)]

#v(4pt)
Dear Pure Storage team,

#v(2pt)
I do not speak French. The posting states that written and verbal fluency in French as well as English is mandatory, so by your own criteria this application ends here unless that requirement can be waived for a German account base. I would rather lead with that than have it discovered in a screening call.

#v(2pt)
If it can be waived, here is what the rest of the letter would have argued. I have owned storage as an operational problem: capacity planned from measured pressure, disk and PSI behaviour recorded every fifteen minutes, restores verified rather than backup runs counted, and rebuilds that reproduce the same system from pinned inputs. I have designed network boundaries — a WireGuard mesh with no public listener, nftables rules at the edge — and I have written the documentation that lets someone else operate what I built.

#v(2pt)
What I have not done is as important. I have never carried a sales quota, run a customer proof of concept, or worked in production Kubernetes and Portworx; my storage is owned hardware rather than enterprise arrays, and my Kubernetes experience is none. This is a pre-sales architect role with a TCV target, and that is a different profession from the one in my record, even where the substrate overlaps.

#v(2pt)
The one part that does transfer unusually well is the economics. Four years managing solar assets commercially taught me to build the model behind an investment case — capex, running cost, yield, sensitivity — which is the language of a total-cost conversation, though not the same as having sold one. I am a German resident with permanent residence, native English and German C1. The repository is public: github.com/shaoyanji/nixconfig

#v(4pt)
Yours sincerely,

#v(18pt)
Matt Ji
